WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:03.840
This video is a first walk through UM-Codex.

00:03.840 --> 00:07.940
You'll open its window, choose a folder, and watch Codex open on it.

00:07.940 --> 00:11.936
Then you'll ask Codex to do something, and stop and start again.

00:13.136 --> 00:17.556
Open UM-Codex from your Desktop, and its window opens in your browser.

00:17.556 --> 00:19.936
Docker is running and your key is saved.

00:19.936 --> 00:23.896
The first time, there's one button: Choose a folder and start.

00:23.896 --> 00:25.976
Under it is what Codex gets.

00:25.976 --> 00:30.976
It can change and delete files in that folder: they're your real files, with no undo.

00:30.976 --> 00:34.976
And the internet is on, so Codex could send what it reads anywhere.

00:34.976 --> 00:36.992
You can change any of that later.

00:37.492 --> 00:41.012
Press it, and choose a folder in your Mac's own folder picker.

00:41.012 --> 00:44.412
For this video, it's a demo folder of made-up files.

00:44.412 --> 00:49.612
For anything important, work in a copy, or in a folder that's a git repository.

00:50.812 --> 00:52.032
That's all you do.

00:52.032 --> 00:55.312
The folder is now a setup, a card named after it.

00:55.312 --> 00:59.132
Its line goes from Starting, to Opening Codex, to Connected.

00:59.132 --> 01:03.612
UM-Codex opens its own copy of the Codex app, with its own settings.

01:03.612 --> 01:06.436
Your own ChatGPT app isn't touched.

01:06.936 --> 01:10.076
Codex opens on a project named after your folder.

01:10.076 --> 01:13.816
At the bottom, it says Remote, and the setup's name.

01:13.816 --> 01:17.056
That chat is running in the sealed environment on your Mac.

01:17.056 --> 01:21.960
A chat that doesn't say Remote would run on your Mac itself, so UM-Codex blocks it.

01:22.460 --> 01:24.900
Now ask Codex for something in the folder.

01:24.900 --> 01:29.100
Here, it summarizes the spreadsheet and writes a short note about it.

01:29.100 --> 01:33.980
Codex works inside the sealed environment, and the note lands in your real folder.

01:34.480 --> 01:38.760
Back in the window, the card always says what Codex can do with this setup:

01:38.760 --> 01:43.912
the folder, and that changes there are real; the internet; and the model it's using.

01:45.112 --> 01:47.052
When you're finished, press Stop.

01:47.052 --> 01:48.332
It asks first.

01:48.332 --> 01:51.172
Codex stops and its sandbox is removed.

01:51.172 --> 01:56.012
Files it already changed in your folder stay as they are, and its history is kept.

01:56.012 --> 01:58.852
The Codex app then says it can't reconnect.

01:58.852 --> 02:00.184
That's expected.

02:00.684 --> 02:05.824
Next time, the button at the top is Start, with your folder's name.

02:05.824 --> 02:05.824
One click.

02:05.824 --> 02:10.004
Edit shows three sections: Folder, Access and Codex.

02:10.004 --> 02:14.508
That's where you add a folder Codex can only read, or turn the internet off.

02:15.008 --> 02:16.568
That's your first launch.
